<title>NORWAY: Bergesen orders $49 mln bulk carrier.</title>
<headline>Bergesen orders $49 mln bulk carrier.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bergesen d.y. ASA, Norway's biggest shipping company, said on Friday it had ordered a bulk carrier of 172,000 TDW from South Korean yard Hyundai Heavy Industries Co. Ltd.  </p>
<p>The ship will be built with ice class for trade in the North Atlantic during the winter season and the contract price is approximately $49 million, Bergesen said in a statement.</p>
<p>The bulk carrier will be delivered in the third quarter of 1998 and enter a 15-year time/charter agreement with British Steel Plc., U.K, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;Our shipping partner through many years, General Ore International Corporation Ltd, has an option to participate with 35 percent,&quot; Bergesen said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
